From 0bc0fabde93d7582a4ba126c2661ba2bf1f969f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viktor Semeniuk <vsemeniuk@google.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:29:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 29/32] [Passwords] Show site-provided credential fields on a
 single line
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Usernames and display names stored via navigator.credentials.store()
are fully controlled by the site and are not sanitized. Several
Credential Management UIs render them in a way that lets embedded line
breaks add extra lines of arbitrary text to browser UI, e.g. fake
security claims:
- The account chooser (PasswordCombinedSelectorView, default) splits
  the lower label on "\n", so each line of the username becomes its
  own detail row.
- The legacy account chooser and auto sign-in bubble render the
  username in a multi-line CredentialsItemView label.

This CL adds GetSingleLineDisplayText(), which collapses control
characters, line breaks and whitespace runs into single spaces and
terminates unbalanced directional formatting characters, and applies it
to the username and display name in GetCredentialLabelsForAccountChooser
(account choosers and the federated save bubble) and the auto sign-in
bubble. The intentional line break between the username and the
federation stays.

Bug: 514008162
Change-Id: If16b375edc8678e59b40914bce8ef4f83a502df0
